{
  "description": "stem-lab/v1, the robot fields of lab=robot (N18 plan 4.7), as one fixture for both sides of the bridge. The simulator (stem-demo src/ui/app/host-bridge.ts) sends only messages shaped like \"valid\"; the host (STEMLearning @stem/api/lab parseLabMessage) accepts every \"valid\" message and drops every \"invalid\" and \"nonFinite\" one as a whole (the house rule: a lab never completes or scores an activity with a message the host cannot read exactly). An \"incomplete\" message is read but never stored: a robot lab does not send one. Kept byte-identical at stem-demo docs/fixtures/stem-lab-v1-robot.json and STEMLearning Web/packages/api/src/lab/__fixtures__/stem-lab-v1-robot.json: change both together, and only by adding (stem-lab/v1 is additive). Blockly and Yolo:Bit messages are not changed by any of this.",
  "protocol": "stem-lab/v1",
  "fixtureVersion": 1,
  "rules": [
    "A robot message carries lab: \"robot\". The host reads the robot fields only then; on any other message they are ignored, never checked (see \"notRobot\").",
    "Every robot field is optional to the parser: left out when the lab has none, never null. One that is present must be within its bound, or the whole message is dropped.",
    "A robot check-result of a scenario with goals carries score, maxScore, scenarioVersion and engine (LearningService refuses a robot result without them); only the goal-less sandbox (goals: []) may leave them out. The host still parses such a message (\"incomplete\"), but stores nothing and tells the learner the result is invalid.",
    "Order: before a check-result the lab flushes any pending project-changed, and it sends no project-changed for edits made while a check runs (the robot lab locks editing during a check). So the last project-changed before a check-result is exactly the checked program, the one programHash hashes.",
    "The host stores a project with a check only when a project-changed arrived after the previous check-result of the same load, or when an earlier check of the same programHash was not stored (refused, failed, incomplete): that check's project goes with the program until one of its checks is stored. Otherwise the program did not change since a stored check, and the check is stored without a project.",
    "A check-result lists the goals of its load's ready: goals: [] only when ready listed none (the sandbox). The host reads a check-result without goals of a scenario whose ready listed goals as invalid and stores nothing.",
    "ready may add scenarioVersion and maxScore; check-result may add score, maxScore, simTimeMs, variants, engine, scenarioVersion and programHash.",
    "maxScore is exactly 100 (every robot scenario scores 0-100). score and maxScore come together.",
    "score is a finite number with 0 <= score <= maxScore.",
    "simTimeMs is a finite number of simulated milliseconds, 0 to 3600000.",
    "variants is a list of at most 10 entries { seed, passed, score, simTimeMs }: seed a safe integer, passed a boolean, score a finite number from 0 to maxScore (so variants need maxScore), simTimeMs as above. Extra fields of an entry are ignored.",
    "engine is 1 to 50 characters of A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ @ - (for example robot-engine@1).",
    "scenarioVersion is an integer from 1 to 2147483647 (a 32-bit int).",
    "programHash is 1 to 64 hexadecimal digits, either case: the hash of the program IR, not of the Blockly JSON.",
    "goals keep their stem-lab/v1 shape: at most 50, each { id, label } (check-result: and passed), id and label 1-200 characters.",
    "Numbers that JSON cannot hold (NaN, Infinity, -Infinity) can still arrive through postMessage: \"nonFinite\" lists them as a valid message plus the path of the field to set to Number(value)."
  ],
  "bounds": {
    "lab": "robot",
    "maxScore": 100,
    "maxVariants": 10,
    "simTimeMsMax": 3600000,
    "engine": "^[A-Za-z0-9._@-]{1,50}$",
    "programHash": "^[0-9a-fA-F]{1,64}$",
    "scenarioVersionMin": 1,
    "scenarioVersionMax": 2147483647,
    "maxGoals": 50,
    "maxGoalText": 200
  },
